<title>UK: Brit Biotech shares calm amid MGAM storm.</title>
<headline>Brit Biotech shares calm amid MGAM storm.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investors in British Biotech Plc, the fast-growing drug discovery group, are reacting calmly to the storm surrounding its biggest shareholder, Morgan Grenfell Asset Management  MGAM, analysts said on Thursday.</p>
<p>MGAM, which saw three of its investment funds suspended this week amid a regulatory investigation, had an 11.34 percent stake in the group on July 23, the last date it declared its interest.</p>
<p>Market-makers said early fears that British Biotech shares could flood onto the market if the funds were forced to liquidate holdings have largely subsided, with the company's shares holding fairly steady so far this week.</p>
</text>
